<DocsLayout title="HC terminal runtime — sum">
  <div class="doc">
    <h1>HC terminal runtime</h1>
    <p class="lede">Use the supported Herdr app and matching HC core. The ordinary agent in its HC-backed terminal is the native lead; Sum provides instructions rather than a transport layer.</p>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Actual lead identity</h2>
<pre class="codeblock" data-language="sh"><code class="language-sh">{`hc --skill
hc run --help
hc send --help
hc wait --help`}</code></pre><p>Require a nonempty actual <code>HC_TERMINAL_ID</code> before inspecting <code>hc get "$HC_TERMINAL_ID"</code>. Confirm the current agent and status against the matching core. Successful RPC connection can start HC’s own core but does not make a foreign conversation addressable.</p><p>Old Herdr TUI pane addresses such as <code>wJ5:p5</code> are not HC terminal addresses such as <code>t10</code>. Report missing prerequisites and use the supported native launch path.</p>
</div>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Launch, report, and wait</h2>
<p>Launch native children through <code>hc run --bg</code> with the inherited parent relationship, notifications, and parent-linked lifetime. Record returned addresses. Include the bounded assignment at launch where supported and inspect <code>first_message.sent</code>.</p><p>Test programs use native exit notifications and inspected output. Interactive helpers save a substantive report, then explicitly send findings, completion, questions, or blockers with <code>hc send</code> to the actual immediate parent. They remain available for follow-up.</p><p>Use <code>hc wait --children any</code> or <code>all</code> when useful. A timeout is a check-in; stopped children or a successful send do not prove completion. Inspect uncertain launches before retrying and never type through trust, authentication, or permission dialogs.</p>
</div>
<div class="sec">
<h2>Artifact and harness limits</h2>
<p>The development host’s observed HC 0.1.17, Herdr app 0.1.12, Codex 0.166.0, and Claude Code 2.1.318 are artifact observations, not qualified minimum versions. Inspected upstream source may be newer than a released binary with the same version string.</p><p>Authenticated native acceptance remains unrun. Claude lead plus interactive Codex reviewer is a candidate qualification path. Other harnesses, including terminal-launched grok, remain unqualified here; the Grok Bot product is separate.</p><p><a href={repoBlob("docs/native-hc.md")}> Prerequisites and observed artifacts ↗</a> <a href={repoBlob("docs/ACCEPTANCE.md")}> Native acceptance ↗</a></p>
</div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
